43: ## Table S5. Decision-curve net benefit (after local recalibration)
44: 
45: Net benefit at threshold probabilities of 0.10 and 0.15 using intercept/slope?recalibrated probabilities, with recalibration applied **out-of-sample by 5-fold cross-fitting**, as specified in ＝2.10. Two default strategies are shown: screening everyone (screen-all), whose net benefit is negative at these thresholds in every cohort except NHANES post at 0.10, and screening no one (net benefit 0 by definition). A model is clinically useful when it exceeds both; the last column gives the margin over whichever default is better.
