194: ## Table S11. Pre-specified selection rules and how they were applied
195: 
196: The statistical analysis plan fixed the primary-model rule before analysis: highest cross-validated AUROC, ties (汁AUROC < 0.005) broken by proximity of the calibration slope to 1, then parsimony. LightGBM and random forest fell inside the tie band, so the tie-break decided the choice.
197: 
198: | Algorithm | CV-AUROC | Calibration slope | \|slope ? 1\| | Inside 0.005 tie band | Selected |
199: |---|---|---|---|---|---|
200: | LightGBM | 0.8396 | 1.0033 | 0.0033 | yes | **yes** |
201: | Random forest | 0.8350 | 1.2034 | 0.2034 | yes | ? |
202: | Elastic net | 0.8220 | 0.9983 | 0.0017 | no | ? |
203: 
204: Other pre-specified rules and their disposition: the parsimony margin follows the plan's recommended 0.02, giving a 5-item deployment model; a stricter 0.01 margin giving 7 items is reported as a post hoc, externally informed variant (＝3.6). The operating point is reported both at the recommended sensitivity ￣0.85 and at the alternative Youden point (Tables S1 and S4). Unweighted training with weighted evaluation was used as the primary approach with weighted training as sensitivity, as recommended. The alcohol predictor was specified in the protocol as current drinking **plus at-risk drinking**, but the harmonized variable uses current drinking alone because the NHANES quantity item was not carried through harmonization; three alternative alcohol definitions are reported in Table S7 and change external discrimination by ¯0.003. The planned self-reported-versus-measured BMI comparison and the prior-depression-diagnosis exclusion could not be run because KCHS records only self-reported BMI and no prior diagnosis (＝4.4). An alternative physical-activity definition was not available in the harmonized data, which carries only the binary aerobic-recommendation indicator, and income exists only as a within-survey quintile. The four interaction terms evaluated in the feature-representation search were specified when that search was written, not in any earlier dated document. The planned R components were not used ? all analyses ran in Python (＝2.12).
205: The analysis was not registered in a public registry, contrary to the plan's intention; the protocol, plan and amendment are dated documents released with the code (＝2.1).

