codex
The central performance values largely reproduce, but that is not the same as the inferential claims being valid. One concrete high-risk issue has emerged: the “oracle” confidence intervals bootstrap a fixed set of cross-validated predictions and never repeat model fitting, so they omit training/CV uncertainty even though the oracle is fitted in the evaluation cohort. I’m checking whether the manuscript discloses that limitation and whether other pre-specified requirements were similarly converted into retrospective checks.
