103: Harmonization cautions: Alcohol, physical activity, and income are measured with different instruments and must be reduced to conservatively comparable definitions; residual differences are quantified in sensitivity analyses. BMI is self-reported in KCHS but measured in NHANES. Marital and alcohol variable names are cycle-dependent in NHANES (e.g., DMDMARTZ vs DMDMARTL). Asian-specific BMI thresholds differ from US categories and are handled by using continuous BMI as primary.
104: 
105: Variables collected in KCHS but absent in NHANES cannot enter the harmonized model; they are reserved for a secondary domestic (KCHS-only) model and sensitivity analyses (Table 2).
